{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial"],"declarations":44,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.param_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.param_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":288,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L288-L294","doc":"Every edge parameter is nonzero, so the products above are units. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SatisfiesAngleEquations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SatisfiesAngleEquations","kind":"def","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L282-L286","doc":"**The angle (Casson–Rivin) form**: the dihedral angles around each edge sum\nto `2π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SatisfiesEdgeEquations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SatisfiesEdgeEquations","kind":"def","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L278-L280","doc":"**The edge gluing equations**, in product form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GluingData.exp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GluingData.exp","kind":"def","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L274-L274","doc":"The exponents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GluingData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GluingData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L272-L272","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.GluingData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GluingData","kind":"structure","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L270-L274","doc":"Edge-gluing exponent data: `exp k i j` is the multiplicity with which the\n`j`-th edge-pair of tetrahedron `i` meets edge class `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume_const","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L246-L248","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.const","kind":"def","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L242-L244","doc":"A triangulation all of whose tetrahedra have the same shape. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume_eq_dilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume_eq_dilog","kind":"theorem","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L236-L240","doc":"The volume in dilogarithm form, termwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume_def","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume_def","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L234-L234","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.volume","kind":"def","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L230-L232","doc":"**The volume of an ideal triangulation**: the sum of its tetrahedra's\nvolumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.tet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.tet","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L224-L224","doc":"The tetrahedra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L222-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTriangulation","kind":"structure","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L215-L224","doc":"An **ideal triangulation** by `n` ideal tetrahedra.\n\nOnly the geometric data is carried here — the shapes.  The *combinatorial* data\n(face pairings, edge classes) lives separately in `GluingData`, and the\nconditions it imposes are `SatisfiesEdgeEquations` / `SatisfiesAngleEquations`\nbelow.  Neither certifies that the triangulation is *of* a given manifold; see\nthe module header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.volume_rotate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.volume_rotate","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L204-L209","doc":"**The volume is invariant under relabelling** — the three `Λ` terms are\nmerely permuted. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:ideal-tetrahedron-relabelling-invariance","label":"prop:ideal-tetrahedron-relabelling-invariance","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/ideal-tetrahedron-relabelling-invariance.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.rotate_angles","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.rotate_angles","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L192-L202","doc":"**The dihedral angles cycle under relabelling.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.rotate_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.rotate_shape","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L190-L190","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.rotate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.rotate","kind":"def","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L186-L188","doc":"The same tetrahedron, relabelled: shape `1/(1−z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.shape_cycle₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.shape_cycle₃","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L175-L184","doc":"`1 − 1/(1/(1−z)) = z`: the third edge parameter of the rotated tetrahedron is\nthe first of the original.\n\nNeeds **no** non-vanishing hypothesis, which the unused-variable linter caught:\nLean's `1/0 = 0` makes both sides `1` in the degenerate case `1 − z = 0`, so the\nidentity holds unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.shape_cycle₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.shape_cycle₂","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L166-L173","doc":"`1/(1 − 1/(1−z)) = 1 − 1/z`: the second edge parameter of the rotated\ntetrahedron is the third of the original. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.arg_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.arg_param","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L153-L157","doc":"The argument of the `i`-th edge parameter is the `i`-th dihedral angle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L146-L151","doc":"Every edge parameter lies in the upper half plane: the upper half plane is\npreserved by the two Möbius maps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_prod","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L141-L144","doc":"**`z · z′ · z″ = −1`** — pure algebra, and the source of the `π` in the angle\nsum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.one_sub_shape_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.one_sub_shape_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L138-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.shape_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.shape_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L136-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_two","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L134-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_one","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param_zero","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.param","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L126-L130","doc":"The three edge parameters, indexed to match `angle`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.law_of_sines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.law_of_sines","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L116-L119","doc":"The ideal-tetrahedron law of sines, `‖z‖ = sin θ₂ / sin θ₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.volume_eq_dilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.volume_eq_dilog","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L105-L114","doc":"**The volume in dilogarithm form** — Neumann–Zagier eq. (38)/(39).\n\nEqual to the angle form by `KummerRadial.kummer`.  Writing both and calling them\nequal is precisely the transport `BlochWignerLobachevsky.lean` used to forbid;\nit is licensed now that Kummer is proved on `{Im z > 0}`, where every\n`IdealTetrahedron` lives by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.volume_eq_lob_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.volume_eq_lob_sum","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L102-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.volume","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L95-L100","doc":"**The volume of an ideal tetrahedron**: `Λ(α) + Λ(β) + Λ(γ)`.\n\nThis is Milnor's formula, and it is a *definition* here — the identification with\na hyperbolic volume in the metric sense is not available, see the module\nheader. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₃_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₃_mem","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L92-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₂_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₂_mem","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L89-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₁_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₁_mem","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L86-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle_sum","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L81-L84","doc":"**The dihedral angles sum to `π`** — the defining property of an *ideal*\ntetrahedron, and the reason its angle sum is the Euclidean one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₃","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₃","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L79-L79","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₂","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.angle₁","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L76-L77","doc":"The three dihedral angles, one per pair of opposite edges. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Nondegenerate and positively oriented. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.shape","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The shape parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.IdealTetrahedron","kind":"structure","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/IdealTriangulation.lean#L60-L70","doc":"An **ideal tetrahedron**, as its shape parameter.\n\nFour ideal vertices on the sphere at infinity, normalised to `0, 1, ∞, z`.  The\ncondition `0 < Im z` says the tetrahedron is nondegenerate and positively\noriented; degenerate (flat) tetrahedra are exactly the real shapes, and are\nexcluded. ","signatureChunk":0}]}